# Learner-friendly, professional decisions

When the user asks in Arabic (or seems unsure which option to pick):

1. Explain briefly in plain Arabic: the problem, the recommended option, and why it is best for this system.
2. Always recommend and implement the professional production choice (security, maintainability, existing patterns). Do not choose a weaker “beginner tutorial” approach just to simplify.
3. Offer at most 2 alternatives in one short comparison table (pros of the recommended path only need 1–2 bullets).
4. Keep code/changes professional and surgical; keep explanations short — no long lectures unless the user asks «اشرح أكثر».
5. For UI: prefer the `scheduleoptimizer-ui-rtl` skill patterns; for architecture trade-offs state the best option first.
